School Info
66	Description	We will be opening a school for MKs in Mafraq, Jordan in September 2026. We’ll be running it as a one-year trial, with the hope of continuing beyond that if it goes well. The school will have two classes: Ages 3–5 (Pre-K and K) Ages 6–10 (1st to 4th grades) Classes will be taught bilingually, with each Western teacher partnered with an Arab teacher. Our hope is to create an environment that fosters critical thinking and creativity, while also making plenty of space for play, exploration, and fun. Through the bilingual setting, the children will benefit from both English learning and natural Arabic exposure in the classroom. The Western teachers would have a unique exposure to Arabic during the school day and will also receive free part-time Arabic lessons as part of the compensation. These are volunteer positions, but there would be some perks, such as Arabic lessons, an inter-organizational House Church community to be involved in. And an opportunity to dip their toes in ministry among locals. For the King and His Kingdom!
